SECTION THREE.ASSESSMENTS: If, atthetime of transfer of title, either Parcel A
or Parcel B, or any part of either parcel, is subject to an assessment or assessments payable in
installments, all such installments not due or delinquent at the time of transfers hall nevertheless be
deemed to be due and payable at such time, and all such assessments shall be paid and discharged
SECTION FOUR.CLOSING COSTS: Exceptas otherwise provided in this Agreement,
closing costs shall be divided between the parties at closing, except that the City shall pay any and
all fes associated with recording the Quit claim Deed to be delivered by the Grogan s at closingwith
respect to Parcel A and except that the Grogans shallbe responsible for any and allfees associated
with recording the Quitclaim Deed tobe delivered by the City at closing with respect to Parcel B.
SECTIONFIVE.RISKOFLOSS; MAINTENANCE; TRANSFER OF POSSESSION:
Risk ofloss or damage by fire or other casualty to either Parcel A or Parcel B, or any part of either
parcel, prior to closing shall be the risk of the current owner thereof.In the event of such loss or
damage to Parcel A prior to closing, the City may, inits sole discretion, cancel this Agreement or,
upon the City's election, the Citymay proceed with the purchase of Parcel A and the Grogans shall
or policies applicable to any loss with respect to Parcel A.In the event of such loss or damage to
ParcelB prior to closing, the Grogans may, in their sole discretion, cancel this Agreement or upon
the Grogans’election, the Grogans may proceed with the purchase of Parcel B and the City shall
cooperate with regard to the assignment ofits rights which are assignable under any insurance policy
or policies applicable to any loss with respect to Parcel B.Possession of each Parcel subject to this
Agreement shall be transferred at closing.
SECTIONSIX.COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS; ZONING; OPPORTUNITY TO
REVIEW APPRAISAL REPORT: The Grogan s warrant that all existing uses of Parcel A are
lawful and in compliance with all federal, state, and municipal laws and ordinances, including
ordinances relating to environmental protection and zoning.It is mutually understood and agreed
that the Grogans, or their family members, have been making use of Parcel B for the storage of
equipment and other materials.Forthis reason, the City expressly disclaims any warranties that all
existing uses of Parcel Bare lawful or in compliance with allfederal, state, and municipal laws and
ordinances, including ordinances related to environmental protection and zoning.The Grogans
warrant and represent that they have no knowledge of anyfact or circumstance that would preclude
the City from using Parcel A for the purposes of constructing and using certain drainage
improvements or for such other municipal purposes as may be determined by the City in its
discretion subject to the terms of this Agreement.The City and the Grogans have received copies
of the appraisal report for Parcels A and B prepared by Appraisals, Inc., Cheyenne, Wyoming, and
have knowledge of the contents there of.
SECTION SEVEN. BROKER'S COMMISSION: The parties mutually warrant and
represent that no brokers or agents have been employed or retained by either party in connection
with the negotiation or consummation of the purchase contemplated by this Agreement and that
neither party shall become obligated to pay any commission of any kind or nature to anybroker or
agent upon the closing of this purchase.
