SECTION EIGHT.NOTICE: All notices required by this Agreement shall be in writing
andshallbe served onthe parties at their addresses, asindicated above, orontheir attorneys at their
business addresses.The mailing ofa notice by registered orcertified mail, return receipt requested,
shall serve as sufficient notice.Notices may also be served by personal delivery.Notices may also
be served by e-mail, or by the use of a facsimile machine, so long as a copy of the notice sent by e-
mail oracopyof the noticesent byfacsimile, with proof of e-mail orfacsimile transmission, is also
sentby regular mail on the date of transmission.
SECTIONNINE.BINDING EFFECT OF AGREEMENT: This Agreements hall not
be binding upon the City until such time as this Agreement has been approved by the Governing
Body of the City of Cheyenne.Except as provided herein, this Agreement, and the covenants and
conditions herein, shall bind and inure to the benefit of the parties, and their respective heirs,
personal representatives, successors and assigns.Unless this Agreement otherwise requires, the
covenantsof this Agreements hall survive the transfer oftitle.
SECTIONTEN.CITY'S OBLIGATION TO TAKE PARCEL A ON AN“ASIS"
BASIS; GROGANS'OBLIGATION TO TAKE PARCEL BON AN"ASIS"BASIS; CITY'S
OBLIGATIONS TO INSTALL FENCING AND A BERM; GROGANS'OBLIGATION TO
REMOVE CERTAIN ITEMS OF PERSONAL PROPERTY FROM PARCEL A; SPECIAL
CONDITIONS: The City shall take title to Parcel A in its present“"as is”condition. The Grogans
shall have no obligation to remove underground utilities or facilities, but the Grogans shall, prior
to closing, remove from Parcel A all vehicles and other items of personal property which are not
attached to the land or which are readily sever able from the land.The Grogans agree to take title
to Parcel B in its present“as is”condition and the City expressly disclaims any warranties as to the
condition of Parcel B or that Parcel B is fit for future uses or purposes of the Grogans, or their
successors in interest.
(A)The City will take all reasonable and necessary steps to ensure that flows from the
8'X 8' storm sewer outfall, to be constructed within Parcel A, shall not enter upon or cause any
damageto adjacent landowners.
(B）The City shall, at its expense, install a sixfoot(6’) chain link fence along the eastern
and southern boundaries of Parcel A to control access from Parcel A to adjacent properties owned
by the Grogans, the Costello Family Trust, and Jina Morandin, et al.
(C)The City shall respond in a reasonably prompt fashion to written and oral
notifications received from the landowners, referenced in subsection(B)of this Section, inthe event
persons access said properties from Parcel A.
(D)The City shall not use Parcel A as a park or public recreation area.
(E)The City shall install a three foot (3') high berm in the location described and
illustrated in“Snyder Storm Sewer Berm, Exhibit C”attached hereto and incorporated herein by
